79. Even in a case coming under (b) where the promissory note is simultaneous with the loan, it is still open to the parties to prove that the promissory note was not regarded as the embodiment of the contract but only taken by way of collateral security or by way of conditional payment. Where a promissory note has been executed subsequent to the incurring of the debt or simultaneously, the question still remains whether it was intended by the parties to reduce the terms of the contract into the form of a promissory note or whether it was intended merely to be a conditional payment or by way of collateral security and that has to be decided with reference to the evidence in each case," The suit as a result must fail;
